  "notes": [
    "Each command has left and right variants. Unprefixed commands default to the right hand.",
    "Alternative packet: {\"command\":\"ui.click\",\"hand\":\"left\"}. Conflicting hand selectors are rejected.",
    "Left/right hand is separate from left/right mouse click: left.ui.rightclick means the left hand performs a right-click.",
    "Placement, movement, adjustment and menus belong to a hand. A screen being adjusted, moved or browsed by one hand cannot be acquired by the other.",
    "Shared commands affect the app or shared screen collection regardless of the issuing hand.",
    "Marker IDs determine left/right identity permanently. Normal centre fallback waits through brief marker tracking gaps; missing markers never borrow the other hand ray.",
    "hand.calibrate is retained as a compatibility status check for the selected root marker. Change marker IDs in the Unity Inspector to change the physical setup.",
    "Use a fresh id per action. Retry with the same id and socket; commands are deduplicated.",
    "appGestures override free-mode gestures only while pointing at the open app face. Timer digits: 10 min / 1 min / 10 sec / 1 sec. Settings, move, place and menus keep their existing controls. Explicit commands are never remapped.",
    "Eleven gestures: aliases swipt_left/swipt_right and wriggle_fingers are accepted. Legacy zoom_in/out still work but are not shown in the gesture panel.",
    "Grab confirms an active edit, selects a menu item, performs the app primary action, or creates a screen on a valid blank surface. Crumple cancels an edit, goes back in a menu, or deletes a pointed screen. It never creates a screen.",
    "Resize and rotate lock the selected screen for that hand. Grab keeps changes; crumple restores the original size and rotation. Move keeps the old anchor until confirmed. Starting a move confirms earlier size/rotation edits.",
    "Timer left/right selects a digit per hand; up/down changes that digit. Without selection, up/down uses the pointed digit (or minutes). Library up swipes scroll forward; down scrolls backward.",
    "Hide the debug HUD to reveal the right-edge gesture guide strip. Point at it to open the guide; point away to dismiss. Works in normal and stereo goggle mode."
  ],
